            0.115,
            0.601,
            0.882,
            0.708
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using the first configuration:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Along each side of the room, the number of balls that can be placed side-by-side along the length is dimension of the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{room}}{\\mathrm{ball}} \\approx \\frac{900}{6} = 150"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". The same number can be placed diameter of the along the width. Along the height, it is 75 balls."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.712,
            0.881,
            0.752
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, 150 × 150 × 75 = 16,87,500 denotes the approximate number of balls that can fill the room."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.756,
            0.881,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using the other configurations, we might be able to fit more balls because of higher packing efficiency."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.8,
            0.842,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Make an estimate based on the second and third configurations."
